content Study cross-coin performance correlation and regime detection.
	
	## Goal
	Understand why some coins perform better than others and identify market regimes.
	
	## Observations from test.sh
	- ZEC outperforms on several datasets (high vol, tight spread)
	- DOGE volatile - both big wins and big losses
	- BTC lower sharpe - too efficient for spread arbitrage?
	- Some coins have zero trades on certain datasets
	
	## Analysis
	- Performance correlation matrix across coins
	- Volatility vs sharpe relationship
	- Spread distribution differences by coin
	- Market regime clustering (which datasets are similar?)
	
	## Questions
	- Should parameters be coin-specific?
	- Can we predict which coins will perform well?
	- Are there coin pairs that hedge each other?
